description:
Split out of task-cb378fd8 by architect-cd0ac706 on 2026-11-04. That row ports PR #208 (`gh.exe pr diff 208`) and needs about 13 files, over the 10-file plan cap. This row is the launcher slice. task-cb378fd8 keeps the docs (README, CONFIGURATION, GETTING_STARTED, SCHEMA), the JetBrains and VS Code labels and the PR hunk map. It depends on this row, because its docs name MOE_AGY_COMMAND and quote the message this row adds.

PROBLEM, at da80b2d8:
- CLI-type detection (moe-agent.sh :639, moe-agent.ps1 :1227) maps only `gemini` to gemini mode. `--command agy` runs claude mode: MOE_WORKER_TYPE=CLAUDE, claude's argv, no .gemini/GEMINI.md.
- The gemini launch block (sh :11611-11618, ps1 :10993-11003) switches to agy only when agy is on PATH. Otherwise it runs the Gemini CLI with agy's flags. MOE_AGY_COMMAND is not read. The message "Antigravity command not found: <cmd>" can name gemini.
- Protected runtime (MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1; sh :956 `protected_resolve_cli "$COMMAND"`, ps1 :649 `Resolve-MoeProtectedCli $Command`): `gemini` resolves the Gemini CLI's absolute path, and refuses when only agy is installed. The block above never remaps an absolute path, so a protected gemini seat always runs the Gemini CLI.
- ps1 calls Write-Error before `exit 1`. Under the script's `$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'` (:125, see the comment at :128) that throws instead.
- Reproduced by architect prototype rows (scratch clone, 2026-11-04): with only a fake gemini on PATH both launchers ran it; `agy` ran in claude mode; MOE_AGY_COMMAND was ignored; the protected INFO line named gemini.

DELIVERABLE:
1. Detection, both launchers: a command whose base name without extension is `gemini` or `agy` is gemini mode (MOE_WORKER_TYPE=GEMINI).
2. Gemini launch block, both launchers, without the protected marker:
   - a non-blank MOE_AGY_COMMAND is the binary (an empty or whitespace-only value counts as unset);
   - else a `gemini` command (base name without extension) becomes `agy`;
   - any other command (agy, a path to agy, a custom one) runs as given, with its arguments;
   - never the Gemini CLI.
3. Not found: exit 1, nothing runs, and one line in both launchers, #208's exact text: `Antigravity CLI (agy) not found: <cmd>. Install Antigravity, or set MOE_AGY_COMMAND to the agy binary path (the IDE may not see your shell PATH).` sh keeps its `${RED}[ERROR]${NC} ` echo on stdout. ps1 writes `[ERROR] ` plus the text with [Console]::Error.WriteLine, not Write-Error.
4. Under MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1:
   - the agent-command allowlist stays claude, codex, gemini, grok, so `agy` stays refused with the unchanged MOE_PROTECTED_AGENT_COMMAND_REFUSED line (JetBrains PROTECTED_AGENT_COMMANDS holds the same four names, task-aa85ff13);
   - for `gemini` the trusted lookup resolves `agy`, never the Gemini CLI (`[INFO] MOE_PROTECTED_AGENT_CLI: agy -> <file>`);
   - MOE_AGY_COMMAND is not read;
   - with no trusted agy, the existing MOE_PROTECTED_AGENT_CLI_NOT_FOUND line names agy.
5. parity-check.sh and parity-check.ps1 require MOE_AGY_COMMAND, 'Antigravity CLI (agy) not found:' and the message's second sentence in both wrappers.
6. Tests with fake binaries only (no real agy or gemini): whole-launcher rows named "gemini mode" in scripts/tests/protected-agent-command.test.mjs (bash, PowerShell 7, PowerShell 5.1), plus `agy` and `C:/tools/agy.exe` typeCases in scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs, which CI runs on all three OSes.

NOT IN SCOPE:
- docs and the IDE labels (task-cb378fd8);
- the ps1 BOM and the heartbeatStop.test.ts flake, already on the branch;
- the protected allowlist;
- the gemini block's banners and comments, and the .gemini/ config writers;
- wiring protected-agent-command.test.mjs into CI (7 scripts/tests files are not CI-wired today);
- closing PR #208, which the governor does after task-cb378fd8.

ORDER: dependsOn CQ-M07t (task-527735ea), the governor's ordering for launcher edits. It also serializes this row after CQ-M07s, which edits parity-check. task-e444f6ae edits moe-agent.ps1's check-dispatch stop area, more than 1,500 lines from these hunks. In worktree mode non-overlapping hunks merge, so it gets no edge.

VERIFICATION: the exact command in this row's plan. It runs the gemini mode rows on WSL node with Linux pwsh 7 and on Windows node.exe, the typeCases, parity-check on bash, pwsh 7 and PowerShell 5.1, and npm run lint.

implementationPlan.description:
scripts/moe-agent.ps1: three hunks, anchored by text. Each occurs once at edc3e937. Keep the UTF-8 BOM and LF endings; the Edit tool keeps both. Check afterwards with ParseFile on pwsh.exe and powershell.exe (step 5).
(a) The protected resolution (~:649), inside `if ($script:MoeRuntimeProtected) {`. Replace '    $Command = Resolve-MoeProtectedCli $Command' with:
    # Gemini mode runs Antigravity only: the trusted lookup takes agy, never the Gemini CLI.
    $Command = Resolve-MoeProtectedCli $(if ($Command -ceq 'gemini') { 'agy' } else { $Command })
This runs before CLI-type detection, so it tests $Command. The allowlist check above it (-cnotin the four names) guarantees an exact name here, and the INFO line becomes 'MOE_PROTECTED_AGENT_CLI: agy -> <file>'.
(b) CLI-type detection (~:1227): 'elseif ($cmdBase -eq "gemini") { $cliType = "gemini" }' -> 'elseif ($cmdBase -eq "gemini" -or $cmdBase -eq "agy") { $cliType = "gemini" }'. A protected seat's resolved agy path then detects as gemini mode too.
(c) The gemini launch block (~:11136). Replace from '        if ($Command -eq "gemini") {' through the not-found check's `exit 1` / `}`; $geminiCheck is used nowhere else. The new text:
        # Gemini mode runs Antigravity (agy) only, never the Gemini CLI, which rejects agy's flags.
        # MOE_AGY_COMMAND names agy when the IDE's PATH lacks it; a blank value counts as unset.
        # Under the protected marker $Command is already the trusted agy (Resolve-MoeProtectedCli).
        if (-not $script:MoeRuntimeProtected) {
            if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($env:MOE_AGY_COMMAND)) {
                $Command = $env:MOE_AGY_COMMAND
            } elseif ([System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($Command) -eq "gemini") {
                $Command = "agy"
            }
        }
        if (-not (Get-Command $Command -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) {
            # Not Write-Error: under $ErrorActionPreference='Stop' it throws before exit 1.
            [Console]::Error.WriteLine("[ERROR] Antigravity CLI (agy) not found: $Command. Install Antigravity, or set MOE_AGY_COMMAND to the agy binary path (the IDE may not see your shell PATH).")
            $script:MoeExitStatus = 1
            exit 1
        }
Why Console: :125 sets EAP 'Stop', and the comment at :128 documents that Write-Error then terminates instead of exiting 1. Console output is one unwrapped stderr line, the same text as sh's. $CommandArgs is kept. Error handling: on a missing agy the seat exits 1 before Start-HeartbeatSidecar and before any CLI, so nothing runs.

Tests: fake binaries only, no real agy or gemini.
(1) scripts/tests/protected-agent-command.test.mjs: append this block at the end of the file. It reuses the file's fixture/run/assertRefused/assertResolved/refusedLine/notFoundLine/show/TAIL/GIT_DIR/nodeBin helpers. A governor seat reaches the CLI with the inert runtime, as rows C1/C2 do. Every row name contains 'gemini mode', which the gate's --test-name-pattern selects. The block:
// Gemini mode runs Antigravity (agy) only, never the Gemini CLI (PR #208's port).
// Without the marker: a non-blank MOE_AGY_COMMAND, else agy on PATH; no agy stops
// with one fixed line. Under the marker: the trusted lookup takes agy and
// MOE_AGY_COMMAND is not read. Each stub logs '<where> <name> <MOE_WORKER_TYPE>'.
function typedStub(fx, dir, name, where) {
  const file = path.join(dir, windows ? `${name}.cmd` : name);
  writeFileSync(file, windows ? `@echo ${where} ${name} %MOE_WORKER_TYPE%>>"${fx.ran}"\r\n` : `#!/bin/sh\necho "${where} ${name} $MOE_WORKER_TYPE" >> '${fx.ran}'\n`);
  if (!windows) chmodSync(file, 0o755);
  return file;
}
const ranText = (fx) => (existsSync(fx.ran) ? readFileSync(fx.ran, 'utf8') : '').replaceAll('\r', '');
// pwsh 7 colours and wraps rendered error records at the console width; match on flattened text.
const flat = (r) => `${r.stdout}\n${r.stderr}`.replace(/\x1B\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-z]/g, '').replace(/\r?\n[ \t]*\|?[ \t]*/g, ' ').replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
const agyMissing = (cmd) => `Antigravity CLI (agy) not found: ${cmd}. Install Antigravity, or set MOE_AGY_COMMAND to the agy binary path (the IDE may not see your shell PATH).`;
for (const engine of ENGINES) {
  const opts = { skip: engine.skip };
  const name = (row) => `${engine.name}: ${row}`;
  const legacy = (fx, command, env = {}) => run(engine, fx, { command, marker: null, role: 'governor', pathEntries: [nodeBin(fx), fx.trusted, ...TAIL, ...(GIT_DIR ? [GIT_DIR] : [])], env: { MOE_NODE_COMMAND: undefined, ...env } });
  for (const command of ['gemini', 'agy']) {
    test(name(`AG1 gemini mode: ${command} runs agy, never the Gemini CLI`), opts, async (t) => {
      const fx = fixture(t);
      typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'gemini', 'path'); typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'agy', 'path');
      const r = await legacy(fx, command);
      assert.equal(r.code, 0, show(r));
      assert.equal(ranText(fx), 'path agy GEMINI\n', show(r));
      assert.ok(existsSync(path.join(fx.project, '.gemini', 'GEMINI.md')), `no gemini-mode instructions\n${show(r)}`);
    });
  }
  test(name('AG2 gemini mode: a non-blank MOE_AGY_COMMAND names the agy that runs; a blank one counts as unset'), opts, async (t) => {
    const fx = fixture(t);
    typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'gemini', 'path'); typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'agy', 'path');
    for (const [value, want] of [[typedStub(fx, fx.custom, 'agy', 'custom'), 'custom agy GEMINI\n'], [' ', 'path agy GEMINI\n']]) {
      rmSync(fx.ran, { force: true });
      const r = await legacy(fx, 'gemini', { MOE_AGY_COMMAND: value });
      assert.equal(r.code, 0, show(r));
      assert.equal(ranText(fx), want, show(r));
    }
  });
  test(name('AG3 gemini mode: with no agy the launcher stops with the fixed line and runs nothing'), opts, async (t) => {
    const fx = fixture(t);
    typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'gemini', 'path');
    for (const [env, shown] of [[{}, 'agy'], [{ MOE_AGY_COMMAND: path.join(fx.custom, 'agy') }, path.join(fx.custom, 'agy')]]) {
      const r = await legacy(fx, 'gemini', env);
      assert.equal(r.code, 1, show(r));
      assert.equal(flat(r).split(agyMissing(shown)).length - 1, 1, show(r));
      assert.equal(existsSync(fx.ran), false, `a CLI ran\n${show(r)}`);
    }
  });
  test(name('AG4 gemini mode: under the marker gemini resolves the trusted agy, never the Gemini CLI or MOE_AGY_COMMAND'), opts, async (t) => {
    const fx = fixture(t);
    typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'gemini', 'trusted'); const file = typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'agy', 'trusted');
    const r = await run(engine, fx, { command: 'gemini', pathEntries: [fx.empty, fx.trusted, ...TAIL], stopOn: 'MOE_PROTECTED_AGENT_CLI:', env: { MOE_AGY_COMMAND: typedStub(fx, fx.custom, 'agy', 'custom') } });
    assertResolved(fx, r, 'agy', file);
  });
  test(name('AG5 gemini mode: under the marker a governor seat runs the trusted agy'), opts, async (t) => {
    const fx = fixture(t);
    typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'gemini', 'trusted'); typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'agy', 'trusted');
    const r = await run(engine, fx, { command: 'gemini', role: 'governor', pathEntries: [nodeBin(fx), fx.trusted, ...TAIL, ...(GIT_DIR ? [GIT_DIR] : [])], env: { MOE_NODE_COMMAND: undefined, MOE_AGY_COMMAND: typedStub(fx, fx.custom, 'agy', 'custom') } });
    assert.equal(r.code, 0, show(r));
    assert.equal(ranText(fx), 'trusted agy GEMINI\n', show(r));
  });
  test(name('AG6 gemini mode: under the marker with no trusted agy the launcher refuses'), opts, async (t) => {
    const fx = fixture(t);
    typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'gemini', 'trusted');
    assertRefused(engine, fx, await run(engine, fx, { command: 'gemini', pathEntries: [fx.trusted, ...TAIL] }), notFoundLine('agy'));
  });
  test(name('AG7 gemini mode: under the marker agy itself is refused'), opts, async (t) => {
    const fx = fixture(t);
    typedStub(fx, fx.trusted, 'agy', 'trusted');
    assertRefused(engine, fx, await run(engine, fx, { command: 'agy', pathEntries: [fx.trusted, ...TAIL] }), refusedLine('agy'));
  });
}
That is 8 rows per engine: bash (Linux, macOS, WSL), PowerShell 7, and PowerShell 5.1 (Windows).
(2) scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs, which CI runs on all three OSes: in `const typeCases = [...]`, add ['agy', 'GEMINI'] and ['C:/tools/agy.exe', 'GEMINI'] after ['C:/tools/gemini.cmd', 'GEMINI']. These cut the real detection blocks.
Architect dry run (scratch clone at edc3e937 plus steps 1-3): all 8 rows green on bash, PowerShell 5.1 and pwsh.exe 7; against the edc3e937 launchers AG1(agy) and AG2-AG6 are red on every engine (AG1(gemini) and AG7 pin behaviour that is already right). The typeCases are 2 green rows on WSL and 6 on Windows (5.1, pwsh 7, Git Bash), and red before step 1(a)/2(b).

